-- NO-OP (repaired 2026-08-06).
--
-- This file was generated by `db:generate` against a stale snapshot chain.
-- Migrations 0003..0008 were hand-written and committed WITHOUT their meta
-- snapshots (meta/ jumps from 0002_snapshot.json straight to 0009_snapshot.json),
-- so drizzle-kit diffed the full schema against the 0002 snapshot and emitted the
-- entire database as if it were new: CREATE TYPE / CREATE TABLE for everything,
-- plus every ALTER from 0004..0008, none of them guarded.
--
-- The result failed on the first statement (`type "payment_method" already exists`)
-- against ANY database that had applied 0003 -- including a brand-new one, since
-- 0003 runs first in the same sequence. drizzle runs the batch in a single
-- transaction, so the whole run rolled back and 0010 -- which adds
-- dresses."currentStatus" and the expenses table -- could never apply. That is what
-- broke dashboard.getData and the expenses module in production.
--
-- Every statement in the original file was verified to be a duplicate of 0003..0008
-- with no net-new schema, so the file is neutralised rather than made idempotent.
-- The file and its journal entry are kept so databases that already recorded 0009
-- stay consistent.
--
-- NOTE: do not regenerate migrations from the current snapshot chain without first
-- restoring snapshots for 0003..0008, or `db:generate` will emit this same
-- full-schema duplicate again.
SELECT 1;
